# Privacy policy: private by default.
#
# Only the public portfolio site is tracked. Everything else --
# IP, agents, planning artifacts, research, drafts, internal
# configs, dev tooling -- stays private.
#
# To add a new public file, EXPLICITLY allowlist it below.
# Do not modify the "ignore everything" rule.

# 1. Ignore everything at the repo root.
/*

# 2. Allowlist: public portfolio pages.
!/index.html
!/about.html
!/work.html
!/services.html
!/consulting.html
!/brand-guidelines.html
!/case-study.html
!/case-study-1.html
!/case-study-2.html
!/case-study-3.html
!/toolkits.html
!/for-enterprise.html

# 2a. Allowlist: CI workflows (nav-gate enforces nav-content + analytics-slot hygiene).
!/.github/
!/.github/workflows/
!/.github/workflows/nav-gate.yml

# 3. Allowlist: public site styling and assets.
!/styles.css
!/assets/

# 3a. Private convention: underscore-prefixed folders are private,
#     even inside allowlisted /assets/. Matches the repo-root convention
#     (_bmad/, _bmad-output/) and catches legacy/draft/scratch buckets.
/assets/_*/
/assets/_*

# 4. Allowlist: repo meta files (added later if desired).
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/README.md
!/LICENSE

# 5. Defense-in-depth: ignore common leak patterns even inside allowlisted folders.
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
**/node_modules/
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/credentials*
**/secrets*
